.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "React Router"
.PP
The \fRreact-router\fP package is the heart of \fRReact Router\fP and provides all the core functionality for both \fR\fRreact-router-dom\fP\fP and \fR\fRreact-router-native\fP\fP\&.

.PP
If you're using React Router, you should never \fRimport\fP anything directly from the \fRreact-router\fP package, but you should have everything you need in either \fRreact-router-dom\fP or \fRreact-router-native\fP\&. Both of those packages re-export everything from \fRreact-router\fP\&.

.PP
If you'd like to extend React Router and you know what you're doing, you should add \fRreact-router\fP \fBas a peer dependency, not a regular dependency\fP in your package\&. 
